{
  "id": "20405_shisaku",
  "headword": "{試作|しさく}",
  "reading": "しさく",
  "romaji": "shisaku",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "prototype; trial production",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "prototype; trial production; trial manufacture",
      "explanation": "Making something on a trial basis before full production, or the item produced in such a trial. Used for products, recipes, artworks, and other creations."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "20405_shisaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{試作|しさく}{品|ひん}を{作|つく}った。",
      "english": "I made a prototype.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20405_shisaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{新|あたら}しいケーキを{試作|しさく}してみた。",
      "english": "I tried making a new cake on a trial basis.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20405_shisaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{何度|なんど}も{試作|しさく}を{重|かさ}ねて、ようやく{満足|まんぞく}のいく{製品|せいひん}ができた。",
      "english": "After repeated prototyping, we finally created a product we were satisfied with.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Composed of {試|し} (trial, test) + {作|さく} (production, making). Used both as a noun and as a する verb. Commonly encountered in product development, cooking, and crafts contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {試作|しさく}{品|ひん}: prototype, trial product\n- {試作|しさく}{段階|だんかい}: prototyping stage\n- {試作|しさく}を{重|かさ}ねる: to go through repeated prototyping\n- {試作|しさく}{機|き}: prototype machine or aircraft\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {思索|しさく}: contemplation, speculation — a completely different meaning\n- {施策|しさく}: policy measure, initiative — used in government and business contexts\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- プロトタイプ: prototype — the loanword, used mainly in technology and software\n- {試験|しけん}{製造|せいぞう}: test manufacturing — more formal, industrial term",
